R11 C029 deterministic hypergeometric-rotor exact self-check
CHECKS=149477
Model: Delta_N=N^-2; rotor phases s=1,...,N-1; exactly s occupied sites among N.
At activation, block labels are uniformly injected without replacement into the N sites.
Exact specified-support phase law:
  h_N,s(i,j)=((s)_i (N-s)_j + (s)_j (N-s)_i)/(N)_(i+j).
Harmonic weights w_N,s=N/[2s(N-s)], c_N,s=(N-1)w_N,s.
Exact finite-N identity for every N>=i+j:
  sum_s w_N,s h_N,s(i,j) = B(i,j).
This is Chu/Vandermonde convolution in falling-factorial form; no Riemann approximation is used.
Uniform visible first-order exit bound: c_N,s * P(nonmonochromatic b-sample) <= b.
